WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.734 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:03.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
is an Emmy, a Tony,
and Golden Globe-winning actor

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from shows
like "Cheers" and "Frasier."

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in the film
"Like Father,"

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.042 line:92%
which is streaming on Netflix.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How'd you guys meet?
-Yeah, what's your story?

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.747
-How'd you catch the silver fox?
-Ooh.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Sighs ]

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Harry, actually --
Rachel's dad.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
Rachel and Owen decided
not to get married,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.257 line:92%
so she invited me to come.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:28.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
You see, I left her
when she was 5 years old.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's unforgivable.
I know.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.767
So I showed up at their wedding
a few days ago,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's when Owen decided
to be a little bitch

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.771 line:92%
and leave Rachel at the altar.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I took Rachel out
and got her good and drunk

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.808 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and, uh, we're here.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.045 line:92%
Kelsey Grammer, everyone.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.813 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:52.819 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome back.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.434 line:92%
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to say this,
and I mean this genuinely.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been doing this show
for a while now.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.773
There's never been a better clip
to explain the movie

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the clip we just showed.
-That's pretty much it.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.377 line:92%
That's the movie in a nutshell.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.178 line:92%
-Not only was it really funny,

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it let you know
who the actors were,

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your character basically
explained the plot.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.150
-Exactly what's going to happen.
That's exactly it.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.188
And the movie is very,
very heartwarming and heartfelt

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.522 line:92%
and very emotional in places.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's kind of
an undercurrent story

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.192 size:88% position:44% line:92%
about Alzheimer's in it,

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.160
which is not particularly funny,
of course,

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it gives it
a kind of gravitas

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.630 line:92%
and an emotional foundation

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's actually --
it's a great movie.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:44.299 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's really fun.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.901
I know a ton of people are
watching it already, which is --

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a big hit apparently.
-That's very exciting.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually --
So you shot on a cruise ship.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:47.707 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had Seth Rogen here
this week talking about that.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.744 size:78% position:39%
But I didn't realize
there was a hurricane

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the lead up
to getting onto the ship.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
Hurricane Irma was sort of

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
playing tag with us
the whole time.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:02:01.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the first week
of the cruise was cut in half

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the ship
wouldn't leave the dock.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.693
Oh, no, it had to go out
into the middle of the sea

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.061 line:92%
and dodge the hurricane...

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I see.
So that's probably safer --

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...without passengers.
-Right.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Apparently, it is.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, hurricanes are not
such a big deal at sea.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're more of a problem
when they hit land.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:17.770 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Right, as a giant boat,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't want
to be right next to land.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You sure don't because then
it ends up on the land.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Yeah.
-That sort of thing.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ]
-Tilted.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.615 line:92%
But it was a fun experience.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've always lived on boats
myself.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up on boats.
I used to own a boat.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's one of the great passions
of my life, so --

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What -- I always am curious
when people own boats.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.593 line:92%
What was the name of your boat?

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, this is --
this has been the subject

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.596 line:92%
of some ridicule in the past.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:46.332 size:81% position:41%
-Oh. Well, I apologize
in advance for asking.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's okay.

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:49.936 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
My boat,

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
my first boat
that I actually bought myself,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:55.375
I didn't buy it
until I was about 32 years old.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
It had been my dream
ever since I was a young man.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I finally got enough money
to buy this sailboat,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.217 size:84% position:42% line:92%
a 37-foot Baltic sloop.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.518 line:92%
And I could single-hand it.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
I practically lived on it
for a few years.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.589 line:92%
But in order to remind myself

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I shouldn't take myself
too seriously,

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.693 line:92%
it was called The BIOYAK,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is an acronym for
"Blow it out your ass, Kels."

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's great.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.137 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.638 line:92%
I think that's really nice.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I feel like
a lot of other people,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.543
when they get their boats, they
name it the other direction.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.744 line:92%
They -- Like "The Winner."

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well -- [ Laughing ]
No, no.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's pretentious
and horrible.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, that's nice.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
And do you still have
The BIOYAK?

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:38.885 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-No, I had to sell it.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.054 size:84% position:42%
Now, this is a kind of
a remarkable situation.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:45.592
I had just fallen in love
with Kayte, who is my wife now,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.593 line:92%
and we have three children

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:49.662 size:84% position:42%
and we've been married
for almost eight years.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.297 line:92%
But I also spoke to her --

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we first met,
we lived in New York.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.167 line:92%
I was doing a play on Broadway,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we spent
most of our time here.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:58.271
The first opportunity we had
to go to California, I said,

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I've got to get you
on the boat.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to come down
to the boat,

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.308 line:92%
and you're going to love it."

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:06.446
So I took her to the boat,
and she boarded the boat.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's standing in the cockpit,
I throw open the hatch,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.617 size:78% position:39% line:92%
went down the ladder,

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm looking inside
down below decks.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And behind me
comes this voice that says,

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Have you ever had sex
on this boat?"

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:23.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:27.400
So I spent about probably
what felt like an eternity

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.968 size:84% position:42% line:92%
was probably 30 seconds

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to run through
every scenario

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:31.904 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that would be convincing

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:35.108
that I hadn't had sex on a boat
I'd owned for 25 years.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:39.846
So I thought, "Oh [bleep] I'm
just going to have to tell her."

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sorry.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:45.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
I turned around,
and I said, "Yes."

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said, "Well,
then I'm not going out on it."

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow! She drew the line.
-Absolutely, so --

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you had to sell the boat?
-I sold the boat.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you get --
-I actually donated the boat.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You donated it.
-To charity.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.464 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, right.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.900 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I thought
what she was saying was fair.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said I could get
another boat if I wanted to,

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but, you know.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When you donated it
to the charity,

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you let them know how much
sex you'd had on it, or...?

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, I did not.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did not.
-I gave it a good cleaning.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I want to ask
because you actually

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
shot this
on a functional cruise ship.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.386 line:92%
-A functional cruise ship.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the largest ship
on the world.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
And because
I'd run boats all my life,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I met the captain
of the ship --

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:27.727 line:92%
because it's called a ship.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:31.197
You know, it's the largest thing
that moves made by man.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.199 line:92%
It's an extraordinary vessel.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.102 line:92%
And he is -- this Captain may be

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:40.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of a hundred guys
in the world

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.774 line:92%
qualified to do this job.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-He is the king of it.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
He sits at the pinnacle
of his trade.

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:49.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, that is a truly
admirable quality.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.550 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he's a terrific guy.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looks after 7,000 souls
on every trip.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.154 line:92%
It's an extraordinary thing.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you get to go into --
is it a cockpit?

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you call where he --
-Oh, no, I never --

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
The wheelhouse or the bridge.
I never went there.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I did go below.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went below decks
a few times to the kitchen,

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is as big as 30 Rock,
practically.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.536
-[ Chuckling ] I can imagine.
-I mean, it's just unbelievable.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:14.941
They serve something like
22,000 buns every morning.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.008 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's a lot of buns.

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
The last time
there were that many buns

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:19.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
was your old boat.
-Exactly.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Just down on the old BIOYAK.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:24.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-The BIOYAK.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:30.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also --
You shot inside a waterfall.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a scene
inside a waterfall.

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's like a big --
it's a waterfall in Jamaica.

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
Getting to it
was somewhat treacherous.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's funny,
I'm shooting a film right now

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.602
where there was some water stuff
we did, as well,

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the same guy
was my stunt double

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:45.671 line:92%
on the film I'm doing now.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:49.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I asked him, I said,
"How dangerous was that jump?"

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:51.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because they wouldn't
let me do it.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.278 line:92%
I said, "I'll give it a shot."

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:54.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"I almost killed myself."

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I thought,
"Okay, that's good."

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.217 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.453
"It's better you almost
killed yourself than me."

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I did have other scenes
I had to shoot,

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:05.191 size:78% position:39%
and he wouldn't have,
so if we'd lost him,

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would have been
a noble -- noble burial.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

